WEBVTT

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:06.534
Captain's Log, Stardate 50460.3.

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.905
We've been investigating
an "inversion nebula"

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.432
for several days.

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:13.105
This phenomenon has never been
seen in the Alpha Quadrant

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:16.946
and is proving something
of a mystery to us here.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:19.383
According to Federation
astro-theorists,

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:22.217
inversion nebulae
are so unstable,

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:25.088
they're supposed to burn out
within a few years, but...

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:27.423
this one appears
to be centuries old.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.690
Maybe the theorists were wrong.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:30.991
After all,
they never had a chance

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.758
to look at the real thing.

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.198
Not entirely wrong.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.701
These plasma strands
we're approaching

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.225
look ready to ignite.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.737
Tom, back us off
2,000 kilometers.

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:40.205
That'll give us a safety margin.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.207
Aye, Captain.

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.607
Harry, set the sensors
for full spectrum scans,

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:44.837
continuous sweep.

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:47.676
If that nebula does flare up,
I don't want to miss a beat.

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:51.751
Mr. Kim, I need your attention
on the sensors.

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:53.946
Sorry, Captain.
Full spectrum scans.

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:55.921
I'm on it.

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:58.321
Astro-theory never predicted
this would be so lovely.

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:03.295
Beauty and mystery...
a tantalizing combination.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.229
No argument here.

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:06.698
Right, Tuvok?

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:09.293
I am fully capable
of appreciating this phenomenon

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.496
without the extraneous
sentimentality

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:13.506
humans find so necessary.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.804
Being moved by an emotion
isn't always extraneous.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.605
Sometimes it's the whole point.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:47.903
Enter.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:51.442
Mr. Kim.

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:53.173
Can I help you?

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:55.204
Um...

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.945
That's kal-toh, isn't it?

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:58.951
Vulcan chess?

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:01.249
Kal-toh is to chess

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.881
as chess is to tic-tac-toe.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:07.256
I should have known.
Uh...

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.124
What is on your mind, Ensign?

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:14.459
Tuvok, I need your help.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:17.629
I want to eliminate emotions
like Vulcans do.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.070
Mr. Kim, it is
a lifelong process.

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:22.370
I realize that, and I also know

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:25.070
that Vulcans use
certain techniques.

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:27.671
The t'san s'at...

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:31.309
the intellectual deconstruction
of emotional patterns.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.983
I'm willing to learn.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.785
May I ask why?

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:43.327
I have...

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:46.389
feelings I don't want to have.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:49.367
That would seem
to be self-evident.

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:51.927
And what is the nature
of those feelings?

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:57.001
I... I'm in love
and I don't want to be.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.578
I see.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:02.479
And who is the object
of your affections?

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:07.617
Her name is... Marayna.

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:11.317
I am not aware of anyone
on the ship with that name.

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:13.018
She's not a member of the crew.

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:17.653
She's a character
on the holodeck.

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:22.326
You're in love
with a computer subroutine?

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:26.134
That's the problem.

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:40.710
Interesting.

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:40.130
To see through
an emotional complex

00:05:40.172 --> 00:05:41.833
is to rob it of its power.

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.739
The first step is to identify
the complex

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.107
in which you have been caught.

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:46.668
I told you, I'm in love.

00:05:46.712 --> 00:05:48.703
There are many different
kinds of love, Ensign.

00:05:48.747 --> 00:05:50.214
You must learn to differentiate.

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:52.479
For example, you told me
that you met this individual

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:55.715
only days ago,
yet you feel overwhelmed.

00:05:55.754 --> 00:05:58.245
I can't get her out of
my mind, not for a second.

00:05:58.290 --> 00:05:59.484
Have you been able to sleep?

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:00.492
No.

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:01.493
Have you eaten?

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:02.494
No.

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:04.655
Does your daily routine
seem somehow empty?

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:06.130
Perhaps even ludicrous?

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:07.826
Yes!

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:09.767
You are experiencing
shon-ha'Iock...

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:10.928
the engulfment.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:12.096
It is the most intense

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:14.368
and psychologically
perilous form of eros.

00:06:14.406 --> 00:06:16.533
I believe humans call it
"love at first sight."

00:06:16.575 --> 00:06:19.442
But... we're talking
about a holodeck character.

00:06:19.478 --> 00:06:20.945
Irrelevant.
The emotional complex

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:22.344
in which you are trapped
is the same

00:06:22.381 --> 00:06:26.078
and so is the cure...
logical deconstruction,

00:06:26.118 --> 00:06:28.951
followed by a regimen
of meditative suppression

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:31.320
as I shall demonstrate.

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:40.627
Uh, a little further
to the left.

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:44.234
No. That's too much.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:45.828
Neelix.

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:50.803
Have you seen Marayna?

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:52.435
Oh... perfect!

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:53.843
Welcome, gentlemen.

00:06:53.879 --> 00:06:55.176
Just getting things ready

00:06:55.214 --> 00:06:57.079
for tonight's
little get-together.

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:59.380
I completely forgot...
the luau.

00:06:59.418 --> 00:07:01.648
Polynesian-style.
I've done my research.

00:07:01.687 --> 00:07:04.588
Uh, Lieutenant Tuvok,
you neglected to RSVP.

00:07:04.623 --> 00:07:06.921
That was not an oversight,
I assure you.

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:08.358
Where is Marayna?

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:09.793
Who?

00:07:09.828 --> 00:07:11.159
She's part of this program.

00:07:11.197 --> 00:07:12.459
Doesn't ring a bell.

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:13.931
How could you miss her?

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:16.434
She's tall, athletic, blond...

00:07:16.468 --> 00:07:18.595
Oh, one of the
entertainment directors.

00:07:18.637 --> 00:07:21.800
I believe she's giving
Kes a hydrosail lesson.

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:24.104
Uh, no, no, not there.

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:28.146
There.

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:31.115
Harry. Tuvok.
The lake is perfect today.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:32.117
Hello, Harry.

00:07:32.151 --> 00:07:33.118
Hi, Marayna.

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:34.380
We were just talking about you.

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:35.444
You were?

00:07:35.487 --> 00:07:37.478
Marayna said what
an excellent student you were.

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:39.388
She's a great instructor.

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:41.825
Ready to get your ears wet?

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:44.328
Vulcans do not hydrosail.

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:45.796
Oh, why not?

00:07:45.831 --> 00:07:47.355
Lieutenant Tuvok
prefers the solitude

00:07:47.399 --> 00:07:49.867
of his own quarters
and a game of kal-toh.

00:07:49.902 --> 00:07:51.460
I'm sure we can do
better than that.

00:07:51.503 --> 00:07:53.630
I'm going back on duty.
Thanks.

00:07:53.672 --> 00:07:54.764
You're welcome.

00:07:54.807 --> 00:07:58.436
There's a volleyball game
starting down on the sand.

00:07:58.477 --> 00:08:00.741
Mr. Kim and I would prefer
some conversation.

00:08:00.779 --> 00:08:02.474
Would you care to join us?

00:08:02.514 --> 00:08:03.845
All right.

00:08:06.151 --> 00:08:08.915
I tried a reverse curl
this morning.

00:08:09.021 --> 00:08:10.318
I think I pulled a tendon.

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:11.345
Feel that.

00:08:13.759 --> 00:08:15.124
It's like a knot.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:16.923
I'm sure it is.

00:08:21.233 --> 00:08:23.326
Are you two friends?

00:08:23.369 --> 00:08:25.337
- Yes.
- No.

00:08:25.371 --> 00:08:26.702
We're colleagues.

00:08:26.739 --> 00:08:30.675
I respect Mr. Kim for his
intelligence and his integrity

00:08:30.709 --> 00:08:33.940
and I assume he holds me
in the same regard.

00:08:33.979 --> 00:08:36.846
So, Vulcans don't hydrosail,
and they don't have friends?

00:08:36.882 --> 00:08:39.908
We have fellowships
and associations,

00:08:39.952 --> 00:08:43.444
but without the emotional
dimension humans experience.

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:46.515
Hmm. You and I are friends,
aren't we?

00:08:46.558 --> 00:08:49.459
Um... yeah.

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:50.757
Good.

00:08:50.796 --> 00:08:52.821
Chakotay to Tuvok and Kim.

00:08:52.865 --> 00:08:54.355
Report to the Bridge.

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.391
Acknowledged.
We're on our way.

00:08:56.435 --> 00:08:58.369
There's a luau tonight.

00:08:58.404 --> 00:09:00.304
You're coming, aren't you...
both of you?

00:09:00.339 --> 00:09:01.670
- No.
- Yes.

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:04.733
You've got to stop doing that.

00:09:04.777 --> 00:09:05.937
Ensign.

00:09:12.084 --> 00:09:13.676
As I predicted, your responses

00:09:13.719 --> 00:09:16.051
were as formulaic
as a mathematical equation.

00:09:16.088 --> 00:09:17.077
What do you mean?

00:09:17.122 --> 00:09:18.419
Consider the expression
on your face

00:09:18.457 --> 00:09:21.449
when Neelix did not recall
Marayna... annoyance.

00:09:21.493 --> 00:09:22.790
That's not true.

00:09:22.828 --> 00:09:23.920
It is quite true.

00:09:23.962 --> 00:09:25.224
At that moment,
Neelix was functioning

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:27.596
in Vulcan terms,
as the soo-lak...

00:09:27.633 --> 00:09:29.624
the third party, who by
his very lack of interest

00:09:29.668 --> 00:09:31.135
trivializes your own.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:33.263
I guess it really did bother me.

00:09:33.305 --> 00:09:34.932
And the arrival of Kes
with Marayna

00:09:35.007 --> 00:09:37.168
then precipitated
in you the k'oh-nar...

00:09:37.209 --> 00:09:39.177
the feeling of being
completely exposed.

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:40.508
I was embarrassed.

00:09:40.546 --> 00:09:42.275
I was sure Kes would take
one look at my face

00:09:42.314 --> 00:09:43.508
and know exactly
what I was feeling.

00:09:43.549 --> 00:09:44.948
And when Marayna
placed your hand

00:09:45.017 --> 00:09:46.177
on her stressed tendon...

00:09:46.218 --> 00:09:48.345
Let's not even talk about that.

00:09:48.387 --> 00:09:49.854
Bridge.

00:09:49.888 --> 00:09:51.947
It's all so... predictable.

00:09:52.057 --> 00:09:53.581
That's just
what I've been trying

00:09:53.625 --> 00:09:54.751
to get you to perceive.

00:09:54.793 --> 00:09:56.385
To the trained Vulcan intellect,

00:09:56.428 --> 00:09:57.918
intense romantic love
is nothing more

00:09:57.963 --> 00:10:00.261
than a set
of stereotypical behaviors.

00:10:00.299 --> 00:10:02.096
Not having our discipline,

00:10:02.134 --> 00:10:04.261
typically, humans are
swept along by the process

00:10:04.303 --> 00:10:05.531
until it ends.

00:10:05.571 --> 00:10:07.266
How does it end?

00:10:07.306 --> 00:10:08.466
Either in conversion

00:10:08.507 --> 00:10:10.702
to a more balanced
stable relationship

00:10:10.743 --> 00:10:13.712
or in tragic circumstances.

00:10:13.746 --> 00:10:15.805
I can't have a balanced,
stable relationship

00:10:15.848 --> 00:10:17.110
with a holodeck character.

00:10:17.149 --> 00:10:18.980
Marayna's a computer program.

00:10:19.051 --> 00:10:21.576
She could never feel for me
what I feel for her.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:22.882
Exactly.

00:10:22.921 --> 00:10:26.823
Logic dictates a single
course of action... retreat.

00:10:32.631 --> 00:10:34.599
To tell you the truth...

00:10:34.633 --> 00:10:36.396
I don't even like hydrosailing.

00:10:41.573 --> 00:10:43.438
The temperature's
5,000 degrees Kelvin

00:10:43.475 --> 00:10:44.442
and rising.

00:10:44.476 --> 00:10:45.602
Captain?

00:10:45.644 --> 00:10:47.305
We've located a plasma strand

00:10:47.346 --> 00:10:48.836
that looks like
it's seconds from igniting.

00:10:48.881 --> 00:10:51.315
If there is
some kind of unknown process

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:52.977
that's been
keeping this nebula

00:10:53.018 --> 00:10:55.111
from going up like a torch,
we're going to see it in action.

00:10:55.154 --> 00:10:56.985
And if there isn't?

00:10:57.022 --> 00:10:58.455
I've got my hand
on the controls.

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:01.220
We'll be out of here before it
even touches our shields.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:03.125
Captain, the temperature
is 9,000 degrees Kelvin.

00:11:03.162 --> 00:11:07.292
I'm picking up a subatomic
cascade reaction.

00:11:07.332 --> 00:11:09.630
There she goes.

00:11:29.588 --> 00:11:32.955
The plasma strand
completely burned itself out.

00:11:32.991 --> 00:11:34.822
Without causing
a chain reaction in the nebula.

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:36.851
Harry, what put out the flames?

00:11:36.895 --> 00:11:39.455
Sensors show some kind
of dampening effect

00:11:39.498 --> 00:11:41.932
between the strands,
but I can't isolate it.

00:11:41.967 --> 00:11:43.992
Like a firebreak in space.

00:11:45.304 --> 00:11:47.465
If we understood
how this happened,

00:11:47.506 --> 00:11:48.734
we might be able
to find a new way

00:11:48.774 --> 00:11:50.332
to contain a warp core breach.

00:11:50.375 --> 00:11:51.933
Or any plasma reaction.

00:11:51.977 --> 00:11:54.275
It's an investigation
worth pursuing.

00:11:54.313 --> 00:11:56.213
Tom, it seems safe enough.

00:11:56.248 --> 00:11:57.875
Take us in
for short-range sensor scans.

00:11:57.916 --> 00:12:00.316
Let's find out all we can
about this phenomenon.

00:12:00.352 --> 00:12:01.546
Aye, Captain.

00:12:01.587 --> 00:12:04.147
I'll see all of you
at Mr. Neelix's luau.

00:12:04.189 --> 00:12:06.555
I'm sure everyone
will be attending.

00:12:20.873 --> 00:12:22.534
Lieutenant,
you look absolutely...

00:12:22.574 --> 00:12:23.905
Tropical?

00:12:23.942 --> 00:12:26.342
More along the lines
of "smashing."

00:12:26.378 --> 00:12:27.538
Thanks.

00:12:27.579 --> 00:12:29.979
Of course, nothing can quite
measure up with this shirt.

00:12:30.015 --> 00:12:32.245
This is an exact re-creation

00:12:32.284 --> 00:12:35.219
of a 1962 big daddy-O
surf special...

00:12:35.254 --> 00:12:36.278
an American classic.

00:12:36.321 --> 00:12:37.345
I'd say you put

00:12:37.389 --> 00:12:39.357
just a little bit too
much thought into that.

00:12:39.391 --> 00:12:40.415
Now, that's where you're wrong.

00:12:40.459 --> 00:12:41.426
Let's go.

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:43.257
I told Vorik we'd pick
him up at 1600 hours.

00:12:43.295 --> 00:12:45.593
And you know how Vulcan he gets
when anybody is late.

00:12:45.631 --> 00:12:46.928
Vorik? I thought
we were meeting Harry.

00:12:46.965 --> 00:12:47.932
Oh, he's not coming.

00:12:47.966 --> 00:12:48.933
Why not?

00:12:48.967 --> 00:12:50.400
He said he was busy.

00:12:50.435 --> 00:12:51.803
With what?

00:12:51.936 --> 00:12:52.925
I don't know.

00:12:54.272 --> 00:12:56.001
Harry and I will meet
you and Vorik at the luau.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:59.134
You're pretty confident
about your powers of persuasion.

00:12:59.177 --> 00:13:01.042
Yes, I am.

00:13:03.881 --> 00:13:05.109
Come in.

00:13:05.149 --> 00:13:07.344
Surf's up, Mr. Kim.

00:13:07.385 --> 00:13:09.182
Hi, Tom.

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:11.814
Harry, this is a luau.

00:13:11.856 --> 00:13:13.323
You look like you're
dressed for a funeral.

00:13:13.357 --> 00:13:14.324
What are you doing?

00:13:14.358 --> 00:13:15.950
Vulcan meditation.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.493
What for?

00:13:17.528 --> 00:13:19.496
To suppress my emotions.

00:13:23.835 --> 00:13:25.132
Is something wrong?

00:13:25.169 --> 00:13:26.727
Not really.

00:13:29.841 --> 00:13:32.105
The... resort woman?

00:13:32.143 --> 00:13:33.735
What was her name?

00:13:33.778 --> 00:13:36.372
Marayna.

00:13:36.414 --> 00:13:37.972
How did you know that?

00:13:38.015 --> 00:13:39.983
For two days now,
every time I look for you,

00:13:40.017 --> 00:13:42.178
it's always,
"He's in Holodeck 1."

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:43.983
And since you don't
like hydrosailing,

00:13:44.021 --> 00:13:45.989
I figured something
was going on.

00:13:46.057 --> 00:13:48.218
Am I that predictable?

00:13:48.259 --> 00:13:50.250
You sound like Tuvok.

00:13:50.294 --> 00:13:53.491
Tuvok? He told you
to do all this?

00:13:53.531 --> 00:13:57.297
Logically,
the best course is retreat.

00:13:57.335 --> 00:13:58.563
Meditation helps.

00:13:58.603 --> 00:14:03.438
Retreat... a classic case
of Vulcan denial, if you ask me.

00:14:03.474 --> 00:14:05.305
Come on, Harry.

00:14:05.343 --> 00:14:08.540
We have all fallen
for a holodeck character.

00:14:08.579 --> 00:14:09.773
It happens.

00:14:09.814 --> 00:14:11.941
You deal with it by staying
with your normal routine

00:14:11.983 --> 00:14:13.951
not by hiding out
in your quarters.

00:14:14.018 --> 00:14:15.451
I'm not hiding out.

00:14:15.486 --> 00:14:18.785
I'm deconstructing
the emotional complex.

00:14:21.225 --> 00:14:23.455
Okay.

00:14:23.494 --> 00:14:25.291
Have fun.

00:14:27.398 --> 00:14:29.161
No, wait.

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:31.725
Computer, standard illumination.

00:14:33.671 --> 00:14:36.071
I'm getting tired of this
anyway.

00:14:36.107 --> 00:14:39.201
Computer, one Hawaiian shirt.

00:14:39.243 --> 00:14:41.143
Specify parameters.

00:14:41.178 --> 00:14:43.373
Pineapple motif.

00:15:11.375 --> 00:15:13.400
Greetings, Mr. Vulcan.

00:15:13.444 --> 00:15:14.411
No, thank you.

00:15:14.445 --> 00:15:17.380
I've done a great deal
of ethnographic research

00:15:17.415 --> 00:15:19.076
on the Polynesian
cultures of Earth.

00:15:19.116 --> 00:15:21.084
The flowered garland, or lei,

00:15:21.118 --> 00:15:24.610
is said to represent
the flowering of love.

00:15:24.655 --> 00:15:26.486
It's a marvelous tradition,
don't you think?

00:15:26.524 --> 00:15:28.492
Marvelous.

00:15:28.526 --> 00:15:29.959
Oh... oh, my.

00:15:29.994 --> 00:15:32.121
Did I program a centerpiece
that big?

00:15:32.163 --> 00:15:33.130
Computer...

00:15:33.164 --> 00:15:34.722
open parameter adjustment file.

00:15:41.639 --> 00:15:44.267
The life
of a recreational hologram...

00:15:44.308 --> 00:15:47.744
dining, dancing,
nonrestrictive clothing...

00:15:49.313 --> 00:15:51.281
I see the allure.

00:15:51.315 --> 00:15:52.339
Your turn.

00:15:57.688 --> 00:15:58.780
Hmm.

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:01.348
Oh, thank you.

00:16:02.693 --> 00:16:04.251
Tuvok.

00:16:04.295 --> 00:16:05.922
I'm glad to see you here.

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:08.362
I would never disobey
an order, Captain,

00:16:08.399 --> 00:16:10.663
no matter how burdensome.

00:16:10.701 --> 00:16:12.100
There's a difference
between an order

00:16:12.136 --> 00:16:13.398
and a suggestion.

00:16:13.437 --> 00:16:14.665
The evening's young, Lieutenant.

00:16:14.705 --> 00:16:15.933
Let's mingle.

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:18.031
Vulcans do not...

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:20.277
Curious.

00:16:20.311 --> 00:16:22.609
What's that?

00:16:22.646 --> 00:16:24.375
If you will excuse me.

00:16:33.424 --> 00:16:35.289
A common error
among novice players.

00:16:35.326 --> 00:16:39.854
By placing the t'an on
opposite sides of the kal-toh,

00:16:39.897 --> 00:16:42.832
you are attempting
to introduce a spatial balance...

00:16:42.867 --> 00:16:44.300
a strategy that will
most certainly fail.

00:16:44.335 --> 00:16:45.927
Why?

00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:48.495
Kal-toh is not
about striving for balance.

00:16:48.539 --> 00:16:50.769
It is about finding
the seeds of order,

00:16:50.808 --> 00:16:53.402
even in the midst
of profound chaos.

00:16:53.444 --> 00:16:55.207
May I?

00:16:55.246 --> 00:16:56.838
Please.

00:17:05.623 --> 00:17:07.887
How beautiful.

00:17:07.925 --> 00:17:09.324
Kal-toh is not about beauty.

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:13.194
I understand,
but... it's still beautiful.

00:17:15.066 --> 00:17:17.034
Did you learn to play on Vulcan?

00:17:17.068 --> 00:17:21.471
Yes. From the age of five,
I took lessons from a master.

00:17:21.505 --> 00:17:24.235
I thought you might enjoy
having an opponent.

00:17:24.275 --> 00:17:27.802
Playing alone must get
a little predictable sometimes.

00:17:27.845 --> 00:17:30.040
You are perceptive.

00:17:30.081 --> 00:17:32.208
Yes, I am.

00:17:32.249 --> 00:17:33.682
Extremely so.

00:17:33.717 --> 00:17:35.344
Aloha, miss.

00:17:35.386 --> 00:17:37.513
Thank you.

00:17:37.555 --> 00:17:38.852
Sir?

00:17:38.889 --> 00:17:41.050
No, thank you.

00:17:41.092 --> 00:17:44.493
You're the only one here
not wearing a garland.

00:17:44.528 --> 00:17:47.725
Given the decor, it
seems somehow excessive.

00:17:47.765 --> 00:17:49.756
I don't believe you.

00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:51.700
I beg your pardon.

00:17:51.735 --> 00:17:53.498
I think you're trying
to isolate yourself

00:17:53.537 --> 00:17:56.506
and make a public protest
at the same time.

00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:57.734
Explain.

00:17:57.775 --> 00:18:01.370
You didn't want to be here
in the first place.

00:18:01.412 --> 00:18:03.903
Being the only one without a lei
sets you apart

00:18:03.981 --> 00:18:05.539
from the others, allowing you

00:18:05.583 --> 00:18:08.143
to symbolically maintain
your solitude.

00:18:08.185 --> 00:18:10.210
And since everybody can see

00:18:10.254 --> 00:18:11.721
that you're
the only one without a lei,

00:18:11.755 --> 00:18:12.915
you're letting them know

00:18:12.957 --> 00:18:15.585
that you'd rather
be somewhere else.

00:18:19.296 --> 00:18:22.026
Your logic is impeccable.

00:18:34.145 --> 00:18:35.373
Thanks.

00:18:39.316 --> 00:18:40.943
Mmm.

00:18:41.018 --> 00:18:43.111
Thanks.
I am starving.

00:18:43.154 --> 00:18:44.416
Oh, me, too.

00:18:44.455 --> 00:18:46.047
Let's find us a spot.

00:18:46.090 --> 00:18:47.455
This place is filling up fast.

00:18:47.491 --> 00:18:49.686
I have already taken the liberty

00:18:49.727 --> 00:18:52.389
of reserving a table,
Lieutenant,

00:18:52.429 --> 00:18:53.987
with a view of the lakeside.

00:18:55.332 --> 00:18:58.460
You did express a fondness
for that particular vista.

00:18:58.502 --> 00:19:00.402
I did?

00:19:00.437 --> 00:19:01.802
Five days ago,

00:19:01.839 --> 00:19:03.170
in a conversation
we had in Engineering

00:19:03.207 --> 00:19:05.437
regarding holodeck programs.

00:19:07.978 --> 00:19:09.912
I guess maybe I did.

00:19:10.014 --> 00:19:11.413
Good memory.

00:19:11.448 --> 00:19:12.676
Of course.

00:19:15.753 --> 00:19:17.186
Well then, Ensign...

00:19:18.355 --> 00:19:19.845
let's go.

00:19:37.474 --> 00:19:39.942
Harry.

00:19:39.977 --> 00:19:41.342
What?

00:19:41.378 --> 00:19:43.346
Do you want to get
something to eat, or not?

00:19:43.380 --> 00:19:46.213
I... I don't know.

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:48.752
Maybe this isn't a good idea.

00:19:48.885 --> 00:19:51.046
Listen, I'm going
back to my quarters.

00:19:51.087 --> 00:19:52.520
Harry...

00:19:52.555 --> 00:19:53.783
Tom...

00:19:57.660 --> 00:19:59.423
Okay.

00:19:59.462 --> 00:20:02.226
Okay. I'll see you tomorrow.

00:20:12.075 --> 00:20:14.942
I like the excitement
of the water.

00:20:16.246 --> 00:20:18.305
The danger...

00:20:18.348 --> 00:20:21.340
being tossed around...

00:20:21.384 --> 00:20:23.978
by the wind and the waves.

00:20:24.053 --> 00:20:28.922
But at the same time,
feeling like I'm in control.

00:20:28.958 --> 00:20:30.653
The illusion of control.

00:20:30.693 --> 00:20:33.491
That's exactly right.

00:20:33.530 --> 00:20:36.727
Because no one can control
the wind and the waves.

00:20:37.801 --> 00:20:42.261
But for a few moments,
when you're on the water

00:20:42.305 --> 00:20:46.708
and the ride is perfect

00:20:46.743 --> 00:20:48.870
the feeling is that you can.

00:20:48.912 --> 00:20:51.107
Do you ever feel that?

00:20:51.147 --> 00:20:52.910
No.

00:20:52.949 --> 00:20:54.746
Never?

00:20:54.784 --> 00:20:57.514
Don't you have an imagination?

00:20:57.554 --> 00:21:00.387
Lf, by imagination,
you mean the ability

00:21:00.423 --> 00:21:03.551
to spontaneously generate
images within my mind,

00:21:03.593 --> 00:21:06.323
then, yes, I have
a highly developed imagination

00:21:06.362 --> 00:21:07.659
as do all of my race.

00:21:07.697 --> 00:21:10.393
All right, imagine this...

00:21:10.433 --> 00:21:13.925
that you, with your logic
and your reason,

00:21:13.970 --> 00:21:19.567
are skimming atop
endless waves of emotion.

00:21:19.609 --> 00:21:20.701
You believe you're in control,

00:21:20.743 --> 00:21:24.543
but you know the control
is an illusion.

00:21:24.581 --> 00:21:29.917
You believe that you understand
the depths beneath you...

00:21:31.688 --> 00:21:35.146
but that, too, is an illusion.

00:21:35.191 --> 00:21:39.958
I can see why Ensign Kim
finds you compelling.

00:21:39.996 --> 00:21:44.194
I can see why Harry admires...

00:21:44.234 --> 00:21:46.498
and respects you.

00:21:46.536 --> 00:21:49.004
Because it's obvious
that he does.

00:21:49.105 --> 00:21:52.597
And... so do I.

00:21:53.576 --> 00:21:56.010
I must return to my quarters.

00:21:56.079 --> 00:21:58.309
Please stay.

00:21:58.348 --> 00:22:01.579
I've never met anyone like you.

00:22:01.618 --> 00:22:05.179
I must admit
I share that conclusion.

00:22:05.221 --> 00:22:08.554
You are a unique individual.

00:22:08.591 --> 00:22:10.115
Then stay.

00:22:10.159 --> 00:22:11.649
It is late.

00:22:11.694 --> 00:22:13.218
I must go.

00:22:13.263 --> 00:22:15.527
Then come back tomorrow.

00:22:15.565 --> 00:22:17.465
I'm sure the weather will hold.

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:19.297
No doubt.

00:22:19.335 --> 00:22:20.700
Please.

00:22:22.472 --> 00:22:23.837
Perhaps.

00:22:25.375 --> 00:22:28.572
Good night... Tuvok.

00:22:28.611 --> 00:22:30.408
Good night, Marayna.

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:46.923
Computer, end resort program.

00:22:53.536 --> 00:22:55.766
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:22:55.805 --> 00:22:57.363
We've completed sensor scans

00:22:57.407 --> 00:23:00.467
and confirmed our discovery
of an unusual dampening field

00:23:00.510 --> 00:23:02.842
responsible for keeping
this unstable nebula

00:23:02.879 --> 00:23:04.676
from going up in flames.

00:23:04.714 --> 00:23:07.877
The field's origin
is still a mystery.

00:23:07.917 --> 00:23:09.578
The dampening field
only seems to appear

00:23:09.619 --> 00:23:11.746
when one of the plasma strands
ignites...

00:23:11.788 --> 00:23:13.585
as if the fire itself
initiates the field.

00:23:13.623 --> 00:23:16.091
Which puts out the fire...
a feedback loop.

00:23:16.125 --> 00:23:18.559
One that's preserved this nebula
for hundreds of years.

00:23:18.594 --> 00:23:21.062
Mr. Kim, do we have enough data
on this dampening field

00:23:21.097 --> 00:23:23.463
to produce one artificially
using the deflector dish?

00:23:23.499 --> 00:23:24.557
Harry?

00:23:24.600 --> 00:23:25.726
Do we have the data?

00:23:25.768 --> 00:23:27.963
Yes, Captain,
but it'll take a while.

00:23:28.071 --> 00:23:30.198
We'll have to simulate
the process

00:23:30.239 --> 00:23:32.173
in the computer
and then try to re-create it

00:23:32.208 --> 00:23:33.641
with the deflector dish.

00:23:33.676 --> 00:23:35.200
Probably a few weeks.

00:23:35.244 --> 00:23:37.405
The project is yours, Ensign.

00:23:37.447 --> 00:23:40.245
Tom, resume course for
the Alpha Quadrant... warp 6.

00:23:40.283 --> 00:23:41.750
Aye, Captain.

00:23:44.287 --> 00:23:47.654
Captain, propulsion
is not responding.

00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:48.816
Bridge to Engineering.

00:23:48.858 --> 00:23:49.882
B'Elanna, what's going on?

00:23:49.926 --> 00:23:50.893
I'm not sure, Captain.

00:23:50.927 --> 00:23:52.417
We're trying
to track the problem now.

00:23:52.462 --> 00:23:53.429
Acknowledged.

00:23:53.463 --> 00:23:55.192
Harry, give B'Elanna a hand.

00:23:55.231 --> 00:23:56.858
The nebula
could be having an effect

00:23:56.899 --> 00:23:57.957
on the ship's systems.

00:23:58.001 --> 00:24:01.664
That's a possibility
we can't discount.

00:24:07.877 --> 00:24:09.174
The warp drive is functioning

00:24:09.212 --> 00:24:10.736
within established
tolerance levels.

00:24:10.780 --> 00:24:12.145
Matter/antimatter containment

00:24:12.181 --> 00:24:13.739
is at recommended
field strength.

00:24:13.783 --> 00:24:15.546
The impulse engines are also...

00:24:15.585 --> 00:24:16.609
Within tolerance.

00:24:16.652 --> 00:24:17.619
Yes.

00:24:17.653 --> 00:24:19.143
Most likely, there's
some kind of failure

00:24:19.188 --> 00:24:21.213
in the computer pathways.

00:24:21.257 --> 00:24:22.690
Nothing's wrong with propulsion,

00:24:22.725 --> 00:24:25.285
but the commands from the helm
just aren't getting there.

00:24:25.328 --> 00:24:27.694
The warp drive seems okay.

00:24:27.730 --> 00:24:29.789
Impulse, too.

00:24:29.832 --> 00:24:31.959
I think the problem
must be somewhere else.

00:24:32.035 --> 00:24:34.435
I think maybe...
the helm's being blocked.

00:24:34.470 --> 00:24:38.736
Like... some kind of failure
in the computer pathways?

00:24:38.775 --> 00:24:39.742
Maybe.

00:24:39.776 --> 00:24:40.834
I just said all that.

00:24:40.877 --> 00:24:41.844
You're not listening, Harry.

00:24:41.878 --> 00:24:43.209
I'll return to my station,
Lieutenant.

00:24:43.246 --> 00:24:44.213
I'm sorry.

00:24:44.247 --> 00:24:46.909
I guess I've got
a lot on my mind.

00:24:46.949 --> 00:24:48.610
Forget about her.

00:24:49.685 --> 00:24:51.482
What did Tom say to you?

00:24:51.521 --> 00:24:52.647
Not a single word.

00:24:52.688 --> 00:24:55.088
I saw the way you were looking
at Marayna yesterday.

00:24:56.159 --> 00:24:59.390
Hi. My name's Harry
"read-me-like-a-book" Kim.

00:24:59.429 --> 00:25:02.057
It's not that bad.

00:25:02.098 --> 00:25:03.497
Apparently, it is.

00:25:03.533 --> 00:25:05.160
I can't get her off my mind.

00:25:05.201 --> 00:25:07.931
Input algorithm not accepted.

00:25:07.970 --> 00:25:09.597
Why don't you take a break?

00:25:09.639 --> 00:25:11.266
I can handle it from here.

00:25:11.307 --> 00:25:14.572
Thanks. I'll be
in my quarters if you need me.

00:25:21.651 --> 00:25:23.084
Deck 3.

00:25:27.390 --> 00:25:29.290
Computer, belay that order.

00:25:29.325 --> 00:25:32.294
Holodeck 1.

00:25:33.863 --> 00:25:37.765
Computer, activate
Neelix resort program.

00:25:37.800 --> 00:25:40.325
That program
is currently running.

00:26:03.192 --> 00:26:04.352
Hello, Harry.

00:26:04.393 --> 00:26:06.725
Enjoying yourselves?

00:26:06.762 --> 00:26:10.960
Now I know why you told me
to keep off the holodeck.

00:26:12.435 --> 00:26:15.893
Mr. Kim, you are misconstruing
the nature of this situation.

00:26:15.938 --> 00:26:18.133
Your jealousy
is entirely insupportable.

00:26:18.174 --> 00:26:19.937
Stop analyzing me.

00:26:20.042 --> 00:26:24.172
I respected you, I trusted you
and you did this

00:26:24.213 --> 00:26:25.202
right behind my back.

00:26:25.248 --> 00:26:26.875
I have done nothing of the sort.

00:26:26.916 --> 00:26:27.883
Then what do you call this?

00:26:27.917 --> 00:26:29.908
A game of kal-toh,
which I am playing

00:26:29.952 --> 00:26:32.113
with a nonsentient
computer subroutine.

00:26:32.155 --> 00:26:34.419
Harry, I didn't intend
to harm you

00:26:34.457 --> 00:26:36.049
and I didn't do anything wrong.

00:26:36.092 --> 00:26:38.390
I'll accept that from her,
Tuvok,

00:26:38.427 --> 00:26:39.894
but not from you.

00:26:39.929 --> 00:26:41.521
You said to stay away from her.

00:26:41.564 --> 00:26:43.054
You should have done the same.

00:26:43.099 --> 00:26:45.329
You're implying
a desire on my part

00:26:45.368 --> 00:26:46.460
that simply does not exist.

00:26:46.502 --> 00:26:48.136
Marayna is an intriguing

00:26:48.269 --> 00:26:50.931
interactive hologram...
nothing more.

00:26:50.972 --> 00:26:53.497
If you say so, Lieutenant.

00:26:53.541 --> 00:26:56.442
Mr. Kim, I value
our working relationship.

00:26:56.477 --> 00:26:58.775
I would not allow a holodeck
character to disrupt that.

00:26:58.813 --> 00:26:59.780
I think it's a little late...

00:26:59.814 --> 00:27:02.647
Tuvok, Harry, please,
stop arguing.

00:27:02.683 --> 00:27:05.083
Computer, delete
the Marayna subroutine.

00:27:05.119 --> 00:27:06.518
Tuvok, what are you?

00:27:06.554 --> 00:27:09.045
That's not going to help.

00:27:09.090 --> 00:27:11.285
I never should have come
to you in the first place.

00:27:11.325 --> 00:27:12.883
I should have
worked it out myself.

00:27:24.772 --> 00:27:26.933
Let's try it again,
Mr. Paris... warp 6.

00:27:26.974 --> 00:27:28.305
Course laid in.

00:27:28.342 --> 00:27:29.741
Engage.

00:27:31.712 --> 00:27:34.806
It would appear to me that we're
not moving, Mr. Paris.

00:27:34.849 --> 00:27:36.214
I don't understand it, Captain.

00:27:36.250 --> 00:27:37.808
Any ideas, B'Elanna?

00:27:37.852 --> 00:27:39.820
Warp drive is still on line

00:27:39.854 --> 00:27:41.719
and helm control
appears to be working,

00:27:41.756 --> 00:27:44.088
but the engines
aren't responding.

00:27:44.125 --> 00:27:45.387
It's possible we've got
a computer malfunction,

00:27:45.426 --> 00:27:46.791
but I can't seem to localize it.

00:27:46.827 --> 00:27:51.230
Let's run a level-4 computer
diagnostic, all systems.

00:27:51.265 --> 00:27:53.130
Aye, Captain.

00:27:53.167 --> 00:27:56.432
Captain, I just got
aft thrusters to respond.

00:27:56.470 --> 00:27:57.528
It's not much.

00:27:57.572 --> 00:27:58.937
I'll take it, B'Elanna.

00:27:58.973 --> 00:28:00.804
Tom, let's go.

00:28:00.841 --> 00:28:02.502
At this speed,
we'll be completely clear

00:28:02.543 --> 00:28:03.635
of the nebula by tomorrow.

00:28:03.678 --> 00:28:05.407
Good enough.

00:28:20.728 --> 00:28:22.457
Your move.

00:28:29.570 --> 00:28:32.266
I think you'll find
my game has improved.

00:28:32.306 --> 00:28:33.773
How did you get here?

00:28:33.808 --> 00:28:35.298
Simple.
I transferred myself

00:28:35.343 --> 00:28:37.243
from the holodeck
to the Sick Bay,

00:28:37.278 --> 00:28:39.508
then used your physician's
mobile emitter.

00:28:39.547 --> 00:28:41.674
I deleted you from the holodeck.

00:28:41.716 --> 00:28:44.276
But you only did that
for Harry's benefit.

00:28:44.318 --> 00:28:47.116
I know you wanted
to keep seeing me.

00:28:47.154 --> 00:28:50.453
I like Harry, but, uh...

00:28:50.491 --> 00:28:52.516
well, you're different.

00:28:52.560 --> 00:28:54.619
You're not like anyone else.

00:28:57.098 --> 00:28:59.828
Why have you come here...
to my quarters?

00:28:59.867 --> 00:29:02.995
You're like a new world
to me, Tuvok.

00:29:03.037 --> 00:29:05.631
I want to know
everything about you.

00:29:05.673 --> 00:29:09.575
I didn't realize how
lonely my existence was

00:29:09.610 --> 00:29:12.044
and I can't go back
to the way things were,

00:29:12.079 --> 00:29:14.479
not without you.

00:29:18.753 --> 00:29:20.914
Tuvok to Bridge.
Intruder alert.

00:29:20.955 --> 00:29:22.684
Security team to my quarters.

00:29:22.723 --> 00:29:23.690
No!

00:29:24.859 --> 00:29:25.917
Why did you do that?!

00:29:25.993 --> 00:29:27.688
Don't you want us
to be together?

00:29:27.728 --> 00:29:28.717
Given your actions,

00:29:28.763 --> 00:29:30.697
I have no choice
but to consider you

00:29:30.731 --> 00:29:33.427
a potential threat to myself
and to Voyager.

00:29:33.467 --> 00:29:34.559
But you're wrong.

00:29:34.602 --> 00:29:36.467
I would never do
anything to harm you.

00:29:37.638 --> 00:29:39.731
Make it stop!

00:29:41.108 --> 00:29:44.441
You have access to the ship's
control systems?

00:29:44.478 --> 00:29:46.639
And I'll use them all
if I have to.

00:29:46.681 --> 00:29:49.172
You can't just delete me.

00:30:02.563 --> 00:30:04.793
Where is this individual now?

00:30:04.832 --> 00:30:07.460
When security got
to Tuvok's quarters,

00:30:07.501 --> 00:30:10.493
she downloaded herself
back into the computer

00:30:10.538 --> 00:30:11.971
and onto the holodeck.

00:30:12.073 --> 00:30:14.735
More to the point, what is she?

00:30:14.775 --> 00:30:16.709
Most likely a sentient
computer program.

00:30:16.744 --> 00:30:18.644
I checked
the Starfleet database.

00:30:18.679 --> 00:30:20.704
This kind of thing
has happened before.

00:30:20.748 --> 00:30:22.511
The Enterprise-D under Picard

00:30:22.550 --> 00:30:25.542
was once taken over
by a holo-character.

00:30:25.586 --> 00:30:27.178
We studied that case
at the Academy.

00:30:27.221 --> 00:30:29.587
It gained control of the ship
from inside the holodeck.

00:30:29.623 --> 00:30:32.183
Marayna may well
have done the same.

00:30:32.226 --> 00:30:34.456
She was able to silence
the intruder alert

00:30:34.495 --> 00:30:35.962
by an apparent act of will.

00:30:35.996 --> 00:30:38.658
Does that mean she has the run
of our entire computer system?

00:30:38.699 --> 00:30:39.996
She may.

00:30:40.034 --> 00:30:41.661
Is it possible
that she is the source

00:30:41.702 --> 00:30:42.999
of our mysterious malfunctions?

00:30:43.104 --> 00:30:45.231
It's certainly possible.

00:30:45.272 --> 00:30:48.264
If Marayna's able to manipulate
the ship's computer pathways,

00:30:48.309 --> 00:30:49.503
she could have
disrupted propulsion,

00:30:49.543 --> 00:30:50.510
and then covered her tracks

00:30:50.544 --> 00:30:52.512
so we couldn't trace the cause.

00:30:52.546 --> 00:30:54.776
But why?
What's her motivation?

00:30:54.815 --> 00:30:57.750
I believe it has something to do
with her feelings toward me.

00:30:57.785 --> 00:30:59.480
In my quarters,
she made reference

00:30:59.520 --> 00:31:01.078
to her loneliness and expressed

00:31:01.122 --> 00:31:04.114
her desire
to continue our relationship.

00:31:04.158 --> 00:31:05.284
But what does that have to do

00:31:05.326 --> 00:31:06.691
with knocking
propulsion off-line?

00:31:06.727 --> 00:31:09.628
Could she be trying
to keep us near the nebula?

00:31:10.798 --> 00:31:12.891
This all started
the day we got here.

00:31:12.933 --> 00:31:14.594
That's when I first met her.

00:31:14.635 --> 00:31:16.967
Maybe the nebula is somehow
affecting the holodeck.

00:31:17.071 --> 00:31:20.268
Giving rise to an intelligence
that doesn't belong there.

00:31:20.307 --> 00:31:21.774
It's possible.

00:31:21.809 --> 00:31:24.141
In any case...

00:31:24.178 --> 00:31:27.705
I can't allow her to gain any
further control over my ship.

00:31:27.748 --> 00:31:31.081
Tuvok, Paris, Torres...
get down to Holodeck 1.

00:31:31.118 --> 00:31:34.679
I want this situation resolved
one way or another.

00:31:41.796 --> 00:31:43.423
She's locked us
out of the program.

00:31:43.464 --> 00:31:45.398
We'll be lucky
if we can open the doors.

00:31:47.635 --> 00:31:48.659
We're lucky.

00:31:48.702 --> 00:31:51.193
Marayna may have
opened the doors.

00:31:51.238 --> 00:31:52.671
Caution is advised.

00:32:01.715 --> 00:32:03.979
I'll try to access
the inside control panel.

00:32:11.959 --> 00:32:13.824
It's kind of creepy.

00:32:13.861 --> 00:32:15.795
Marayna's attempting
to re-create the setting

00:32:15.830 --> 00:32:17.491
of my previous
encounter with her.

00:32:17.531 --> 00:32:20.091
You really know
how to pick them, Tuvok.

00:32:26.674 --> 00:32:29.370
I got access
to the holodeck computer.

00:32:29.410 --> 00:32:32.174
I'm not reading anything
unusual on the holodeck.

00:32:32.213 --> 00:32:34.579
It seems to be
working perfectly.

00:32:34.615 --> 00:32:38.073
There's a subspace signal coming
from outside of Voyager.

00:32:38.118 --> 00:32:40.018
It's some kind of an uplink.

00:32:41.322 --> 00:32:43.882
There's somebody on a ship
out there tapping into the...

00:32:44.925 --> 00:32:46.916
B'Elanna!

00:33:18.592 --> 00:33:20.025
Shoot the control panel.

00:33:48.722 --> 00:33:49.484
Shield status?

00:33:49.523 --> 00:33:50.723
Still holding, Captain,

00:33:50.856 --> 00:33:53.689
but the inertial
dampeners are off-line.

00:33:53.726 --> 00:33:56.923
Starboard shields are
down to 80 percent.

00:33:56.962 --> 00:33:58.259
What happened down there?

00:33:58.297 --> 00:34:00.492
Marayna attacked us
and attempted to restrain me.

00:34:00.532 --> 00:34:02.329
She has control
over the holodeck characters.

00:34:02.367 --> 00:34:04.426
But she's not actually
on the holodeck.

00:34:04.470 --> 00:34:06.233
I found an uplink
and tracked it to the nebula.

00:34:06.271 --> 00:34:08.262
She's on a hidden ship
or a space station.

00:34:08.307 --> 00:34:11.367
She's manipulating
the holodeck from there.

00:34:11.410 --> 00:34:13.503
She's been using the Marayna
character like a puppet.

00:34:13.545 --> 00:34:14.944
As an interface.

00:34:15.013 --> 00:34:17.607
A way to move around Voyager
to interact with us.

00:34:17.649 --> 00:34:20.516
Tuvok, come back to me.

00:34:20.552 --> 00:34:22.110
I'm waiting for you.

00:34:22.154 --> 00:34:24.281
Harry, try to trace the uplink.

00:34:24.323 --> 00:34:25.620
Find her.

00:34:25.657 --> 00:34:30.390
Don't make this more difficult
than it already is, Captain.

00:34:30.429 --> 00:34:32.954
Are you responsible
for the plasma fires?

00:34:32.998 --> 00:34:36.798
You're giving me no other choice
but to force the issue.

00:34:36.835 --> 00:34:38.769
What do you want?

00:34:38.804 --> 00:34:40.965
Tuvok.

00:34:41.006 --> 00:34:42.530
I want Tuvok.

00:34:42.574 --> 00:34:45.566
Let him come to the holodeck
alone

00:34:45.611 --> 00:34:47.670
or I'll destroy your ship.

00:35:05.764 --> 00:35:07.459
Tuvok.

00:35:07.499 --> 00:35:08.966
You're back.

00:35:11.370 --> 00:35:12.735
I had little choice.

00:35:12.771 --> 00:35:14.295
We're alone now.

00:35:17.843 --> 00:35:20.641
No one can see us or hear us.

00:35:20.679 --> 00:35:23.204
We can do whatever we want.

00:35:23.248 --> 00:35:25.580
You don't have
to pretend anymore.

00:35:25.617 --> 00:35:28.484
This is our world.

00:35:28.520 --> 00:35:30.112
You've successfully
lured me here

00:35:30.155 --> 00:35:31.349
by threatening the ship.

00:35:31.390 --> 00:35:34.382
But any attempt to generate
intimacy between us

00:35:34.426 --> 00:35:36.485
will not be successful.

00:35:36.528 --> 00:35:38.860
I've isolated the source
of the uplink signal.

00:35:38.897 --> 00:35:40.524
Stand by to transport.

00:35:42.434 --> 00:35:44.959
I understand your sense of duty,

00:35:45.070 --> 00:35:46.697
of loyalty to your Captain,

00:35:46.738 --> 00:35:49.229
but we have something stronger...

00:35:49.274 --> 00:35:51.765
a connection that goes
beyond duty and loyalty.

00:35:53.345 --> 00:35:55.836
I know you want
to be with me, Tuvok.

00:35:55.881 --> 00:35:58.714
You must leave Voyager now

00:35:58.750 --> 00:36:01.014
and allow us to continue
on our course.

00:36:01.053 --> 00:36:02.816
I won't.

00:36:02.855 --> 00:36:04.550
I suggest you reconsider

00:36:04.590 --> 00:36:07.650
or Captain Janeway will be
forced to take action.

00:36:07.693 --> 00:36:09.627
There's nothing she can do.

00:36:09.661 --> 00:36:11.891
You're staying here with me.

00:36:11.930 --> 00:36:14.831
She'll just have to accept that.

00:36:17.736 --> 00:36:19.294
Energize.

00:36:19.338 --> 00:36:21.533
Transporting to the source
of the uplink.

00:36:21.573 --> 00:36:22.801
Stop!

00:36:32.651 --> 00:36:34.812
Shields are down to 47 percent.

00:37:01.847 --> 00:37:02.814
Shields are gone.

00:37:02.848 --> 00:37:04.247
Try to hail Tuvok.

00:37:04.283 --> 00:37:05.409
I can't, Captain.

00:37:05.450 --> 00:37:07.281
Something's blocking the signal.

00:37:28.206 --> 00:37:29.332
Marayna?

00:37:31.710 --> 00:37:34.702
Your ship is helpless.

00:37:34.746 --> 00:37:40.343
If I ignite one more strand,
the hull will fail.

00:37:42.821 --> 00:37:45.517
You are using
the nebula as a weapon.

00:37:45.557 --> 00:37:47.650
My nebula.

00:37:47.693 --> 00:37:49.957
I will fire if necessary.

00:37:50.062 --> 00:37:51.359
You're too late.

00:37:51.396 --> 00:37:53.887
I've already set
the ignition sequence.

00:37:53.932 --> 00:37:56.901
Only I can stop it.

00:38:04.009 --> 00:38:05.738
Are you alone here...

00:38:05.777 --> 00:38:07.904
on this station...

00:38:07.980 --> 00:38:09.607
in this nebula?

00:38:09.648 --> 00:38:11.775
Yes.

00:38:11.817 --> 00:38:13.785
It's my work.

00:38:13.819 --> 00:38:15.582
I don't understand.

00:38:18.323 --> 00:38:22.316
I keep the plasma fires
from chain-reacting.

00:38:22.361 --> 00:38:24.761
You are responsible
for the dampening field

00:38:24.796 --> 00:38:27.128
we've been investigating.

00:38:27.165 --> 00:38:28.826
That's correct.

00:38:28.867 --> 00:38:32.200
I generate it from here
to preserve the nebula,

00:38:32.237 --> 00:38:35.968
so that others from my home
planet may enjoy its beauty.

00:38:39.277 --> 00:38:42.110
I watch the ships
when they pass by.

00:38:42.147 --> 00:38:45.446
They don't even know I'm here.

00:38:46.985 --> 00:38:50.216
You are... lonely.

00:38:51.923 --> 00:38:54.323
By choice.

00:38:54.359 --> 00:38:58.693
I prefer to be here... alone.

00:38:58.730 --> 00:39:00.960
But you uplinked
with our holodeck

00:39:00.999 --> 00:39:03.900
and created a character
in order to interact with us.

00:39:03.935 --> 00:39:05.129
To amuse myself.

00:39:05.170 --> 00:39:06.762
I've done it before...

00:39:06.805 --> 00:39:09.672
tapped into the computer
of a passing alien vessel,

00:39:09.708 --> 00:39:13.405
examined all the little details
of their lives.

00:39:15.080 --> 00:39:21.280
But I never expected to find
something as... diverting

00:39:21.319 --> 00:39:23.549
as your holodeck.

00:39:23.588 --> 00:39:26.887
I never expected to find you.

00:39:26.925 --> 00:39:29.450
You...

00:39:29.494 --> 00:39:33.362
are like nothing else
I've ever encountered.

00:39:36.368 --> 00:39:38.233
And I can't be without you.

00:39:42.474 --> 00:39:44.567
Stay here with me

00:39:44.609 --> 00:39:47.635
and I will let
your ship resume course.

00:39:48.847 --> 00:39:51.247
If it is the only option,

00:39:51.283 --> 00:39:55.515
I would willingly sacrifice
myself to save my crewmates.

00:39:55.554 --> 00:39:57.249
No, that's not enough.

00:39:57.289 --> 00:39:59.280
You have to want to be with me.

00:39:59.324 --> 00:40:02.225
If you truly understood
who and what I am,

00:40:02.260 --> 00:40:04.922
you would know that I could
never return your affections.

00:40:04.963 --> 00:40:10.697
But... you are more like me
than-than you are like them.

00:40:10.735 --> 00:40:13.966
I-I-I've seen the way
you isolate yourself.

00:40:14.005 --> 00:40:18.465
Even in a crowd of people,
you're alone.

00:40:18.510 --> 00:40:20.808
We should be together.

00:40:21.813 --> 00:40:23.940
I must admit...

00:40:23.982 --> 00:40:26.348
I found our conversation
stimulating,

00:40:26.384 --> 00:40:33.153
your insight and intelligence
fresh and unexpected.

00:40:33.191 --> 00:40:35.716
In other circumstances,

00:40:35.760 --> 00:40:38.888
I would be willing to spend
time in your company

00:40:38.930 --> 00:40:43.629
to continue to share
knowledge and ideas,

00:40:43.668 --> 00:40:49.300
but I have a home
and a spouse on Vulcan.

00:40:49.341 --> 00:40:53.471
I have a mission,
and colleagues who depend on me.

00:40:56.715 --> 00:41:00.549
I do not have a complete
understanding of emotions,

00:41:00.585 --> 00:41:06.024
but I believe
that if you truly care for me,

00:41:06.157 --> 00:41:09.593
you will not pursue
this course of action.

00:41:29.580 --> 00:41:31.775
You may go.

00:41:37.522 --> 00:41:40.855
Your communicator
will function now.

00:41:43.694 --> 00:41:44.991
Tuvok to Voyager.

00:41:45.096 --> 00:41:47.428
Go ahead, Tuvok.

00:41:47.465 --> 00:41:49.831
I am ready to return.

00:41:49.867 --> 00:41:52.700
Stand by to beam me aboard.

00:41:56.741 --> 00:41:59.710
Captain, ship's systems
are coming back on line.

00:41:59.744 --> 00:42:01.769
Acknowledged, Tuvok.

00:42:01.813 --> 00:42:03.212
Standing by.

00:42:06.984 --> 00:42:09.384
Consider this:

00:42:09.420 --> 00:42:11.149
Your feelings toward me

00:42:11.189 --> 00:42:14.386
may be evidence
of a deeper need...

00:42:14.425 --> 00:42:18.521
a more...
profound loneliness

00:42:18.563 --> 00:42:20.861
than you are willing to admit.

00:42:20.898 --> 00:42:25.562
Why don't you call
for a replacement?

00:42:25.603 --> 00:42:28.299
Let another occupy this task.

00:42:28.339 --> 00:42:33.140
Attempt for a time
to live among your own kind.

00:42:38.015 --> 00:42:42.679
Logically, that would be
the best thing to do.

00:42:42.720 --> 00:42:45.518
Yes.

00:42:45.556 --> 00:42:48.081
Perhaps I will.

00:42:54.532 --> 00:42:56.090
Tuvok to Voyager.

00:42:56.134 --> 00:42:57.692
Ready for transport.

00:42:57.735 --> 00:43:00.761
But what about you, Tuvok?

00:43:00.805 --> 00:43:03.365
Will you always be alone?

00:43:14.852 --> 00:43:19.186
Security Chief's Log,
Stardate 50471.3.

00:43:19.223 --> 00:43:21.714
The remaining damage
to the ship was easily repaired

00:43:21.759 --> 00:43:24.353
and we soon left
Marayna's nebula behind.

00:43:24.395 --> 00:43:26.056
Voyager is back on course

00:43:26.097 --> 00:43:28.497
and I have resumed
my normal routine.

00:43:53.591 --> 00:43:55.320
Mr. Kim.

00:43:55.359 --> 00:43:58.522
Would you be interested
in learning to play kal-toh?

00:44:00.331 --> 00:44:04.131
I thought kal-toh was
beyond human understanding.

00:44:05.803 --> 00:44:06.963
Not entirely.

00:44:12.677 --> 00:44:14.872
Ensign...

00:44:14.912 --> 00:44:20.509
I failed to respect
the complexity of your emotions.

00:44:21.986 --> 00:44:25.581
I apologize
for my lack of consideration.

00:44:28.626 --> 00:44:30.753
Don't worry about it, Tuvok.

00:44:30.795 --> 00:44:33.127
Apology accepted.

00:44:41.005 --> 00:44:43.200
Won't this take years to learn?

00:44:43.241 --> 00:44:45.505
It will, indeed.

00:44:45.543 --> 00:44:46.976
May I join you?

00:44:47.011 --> 00:44:48.376
- No.
- No.

00:44:48.412 --> 00:44:51.176
But... thank you.
